cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use grainsmith in published work, please cite it together with the
  references below (Voronoi construction ancestry, uniform SO(3) sampling,
  misorientation statistics, the CSL angular criterion, self-affine
  grain-boundary roughness, and grain-boundary curvature).
title: "grainsmith: A Generator of Polycrystalline Models for Atomistic
  Simulations with Statistical and Grain-Boundary Morphology Control"
authors:
  - family-names: Orhan
    given-names: Oğuzhan
    email: oguzhan.orhan@firat.edu.tr
    affiliation: "Department of Physics, Fırat University, Elazığ, Türkiye"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2049-053X"
  - family-names: Özgen
    given-names: Soner
    affiliation: "Department of Physics, Fırat University, Elazığ, Türkiye"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4292-9187"
type: software
version: 1.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-19
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/oguzhanorhan/grainsmith"
abstract: >-
  grainsmith builds periodic or slab polycrystalline (and multiphase and
  single-crystal) atomistic models for molecular dynamics, with statistically
  controlled microstructure. It supports all 230 space groups via spglib; flat
  (Qhull Voronoi), volume-targeted Laguerre/power (semi-discrete optimal
  transport), curved (domain-warped, additive-weight, anisotropic) and
  self-affine (fractal) grain boundaries; ODF texture components and MDF
  boundary-network targeting; multiphase volume-fraction partitioning;
  voxel-field (DREAM.3D/.npy) import; deterministic seeded generation with
  construction-time QA gates; and publication-grade outputs (statistics,
  machine-readable record, auto-generated methods) including grain-boundary
  character and cubic CSL sigma assignment under the Brandon criterion.
keywords:
  - molecular-dynamics
  - polycrystal
  - voronoi
  - laguerre-tessellation
  - optimal-transport
  - texture
  - grain-boundary
  - space-group
  - LAMMPS
